+# Loom P coupling-commissioning apparatus — construction review
+
+Date: 2026-09-24. P implementation: `6bc9683b54e4fa80136fe8534d7713e2a250a95f`.
+
+**Apparatus construction and bounded component verification complete. Commissioning has not begun or been authorized.** The P runtime and configuration are unchanged. This apparatus needs independent review before commissioning execution. P retains its prior scoped engineering-fidelity disposition and remains scientifically uncommissioned/untested.
+
+The isolated worktree is `C:\Users\Jason\Desktop\Eridos\Loom-p-apparatus-20260924-01a0c405`, branch `build/p-commissioning-apparatus-20260924-01a0c405`. The portable package's `CHECKPOINT.json` gives the final local commit, its parent, exact binary diff and code identities without a self-referential commit claim in this committed document.
+
+## Implemented apparatus
+
+`developmental_ecology/loom_commissioning` is a separate package. No file in `loom_p`, no P parameter, and no earlier engineering test was edited. Eight units per sensory cortex, two pools, mean-plus-endpoint packets, both centring operations, contracting association, separate E/I credit and all other P laws remain intact. R and all alternatives remain preserved.
+
+The manifest requires exact P, configuration and apparatus identities; a complete initial-state identity; phase/field provenance; a fixed duration and absolute deadline; controller/trajectory identity; predetermined D5 selection; and the unstarted birth roster. It supports the design's horizons through 1,200 seconds. Intact P advances through the original `Engine.step`. The external and fixed-structure adapters retain its native/field/terminal schedule with their declared interventions. No runner calls the old 30-second bounded function repeatedly.
+
+Commands in external arms are held for ten native steps. A pause between decisions does not advance any clock or random stream. A pause at step seven retains the remaining three held steps across restart. The original deadline, controller state, frozen structure, sensor history, random state, body, chemistry and neural state survive in the restart record. Only a completed administrative pause resumes. A cutoff, terminal state, incomplete stream or apparatus failure cannot silently restart. A new output segment preserves the prior segment and its manifest hash. The periodic snapshot trigger was exercised at the manufactured 1,200-second clock endpoint; a continuing ten-second checkpoint series was not run.
+
+The physical-ceiling controller is a deterministic prescribed-waypoint/wait/contact-force-feedback controller. Its input schema is closed to the design's privileged geometry/body/stock/contact/clock list. It receives copied values and returns only two bounded actuator commands. Its initial controller constants are disclosed in code; they were not tuned on outcomes. Its route-following capability for A1–A5 is **not established**. Manual privileged command entry remains an API fallback, recorded as external control.
+
+The human sensor interface receives only the 29 raw coordinates, their history, held actual E/I at the native wave cadence, and the operator's commands/notes. The loopback server has no evaluation, manifest, file-serving, pose or world-setting endpoint. Privileged exceptions are not returned to the operator. A separate offline evaluator reads physical and neural records. An operator who has inspected those privileged records cannot supply a blinded witness for that fixture.
+
+The **FIXED-STRUCTURE / NO-LASTING-PLASTICITY DIAGNOSTIC** freezes sensory `shared`, `fine`, `shared_ref`, `fine_ref`; association `H` and `use`; and regulator `theta` and `reference`. It requires newborn structure. Bank restoration occurs between credit and control production; sensory fields are restored immediately after native operations; maps/use are restored after their hypothetical write and before any next read. Transient states continue. Hypothetical updates remain inspectable and the applied structural increment is explicitly zero. This arm is never labelled intact P and supplies no innate-performance proof.
+
+Every native sample retains aligned step-start raw, receptor mean/residual, activity, shared/fine pressure, references, support, opening and applied increments. Every wave retains packet/mean/beta/trace/query alignment, association contributions and separate E/I credit operands. D5 evaluates every handoff; native-only motor probes use `native_index % 100 == 0`, with motor reconstruction also at every handoff. Selection is fixed before any magnitudes are read. Detached receivers reconstruct the original output before removing one contribution, including recomputing query/support read dependencies. They consume no live random draws. There is no gain normalization or alternate behavioral trajectory.
+
+AV and CO are the commissioning review surface. SO observations have a separate preserved stream and cannot pass `configuration_grounds`. That API produces a request for Jason's defect-specific decision; it cannot adjust configuration. The four proposed birth IDs and 600-second ceilings remain in every manifest. Zero witnesses at that coverage means unresolved opportunity; no extension rule exists.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+The final worktree suite passed **83 tests in 34.18 seconds**: 24 apparatus checks and all 59 unchanged P component checks. All **16 observed RED→GREEN pairs** reached their intended fault, including separate native, wave, random and field interventions. Full logs and commands are in `faults-attempt-002/FAULT_MATRIX.json`. The fully assembled portable package also passed **83 tests in 58.63 seconds**, recorded separately in `portable-suite.log`.
+
+The new fixtures are manufactured, not lawful ecological births: zero initial chemical fields, phase zero, a disclosed body state at `[5,5]`, and explicitly manufactured clock/state variants. Normal recorded components last 0.2 seconds; controller checks last 0.1 seconds. A partial-terminal fixture uses a manufactured small energy reserve. One manufactured native step begins at clock 1,199.99 seconds; another at 31.99 seconds tests P's due wave. These are clock-boundary components, not 1,200- or 32-second lives. A 1,200-second manifest with the existing verified life-0 cache was validated and its unauthorized execution rejected before output creation. No new prehistory was prepared, and life-0 history was not reused for births 1–4.
+
+The fixed-structure poison fixture changes discarded sensory, bank, map and use updates while keeping their ordinary transient operations. With correct restoration, all subsequent causal state and RNG match. A deliberately late bank restoration leaves frozen parameters restored but changes subsequent output/state; it fails the intended assertion. Receiver checks also use manufactured nonzero maps/banks so q and removal sensitivity are not tested only at their zero birth values.
+
+All three recorded modes reproduce their complete native, wave, event and final field/neural state from saved initial states. Paused and continuous paths agree. Recorded sensor histories are compared against reconstructed physical transduction and held E/I, not merely checked for field names. Source debit, body credit, renewal, expenditure, damage and restoration are balanced. No useful behavior, learning or survival threshold is a pass condition.
+
+Development history is retained: the first apparatus suite had one validator error (`E/I` versus P's actual `energy/integrity` terminal names); the next combined run lacked the existing prehistory cache in the fresh worktree, producing five setup failures. Correcting the validator and copying the unchanged cache resolved those failures. A packaging-only directory glob and archive-manifest filename were corrected before package completion; neither affected P or the apparatus runtime. Earlier logs and evidence were not erased.
+
+The sensor display was inspected in the browser and its history slider verified: at 0.100 seconds, E/I still show their 0.000-second sample; at 0.200 seconds, the new sample appears. The apply button is disabled in saved review. The temporary server was stopped. Browser security blocked direct `file:` navigation, so native double-click execution was not automated. The static launch targets and their embedded saved payloads were checked. `UI_REVIEW.json` preserves that limitation.
+
+## Runtime, storage and execution boundary
+
+The 0.2-second components cost 2.44–3.03 wall seconds including recorder/snapshot and diagnostic overhead. Intact P's stored record set is 960,238 bytes; fixed structure is 598,918 bytes; external control is 156,375 bytes. These are short component measurements, **not steady-state lifetime rates**. Applying the largest observed rates to the previously proposed 8,960-second workload gives a provisional envelope of about **37.74 machine-hours and 43.02 GB stored**, or about 86.04 GB with one duplicate. This does not authorize that workload or budget and is not a calibrated performance forecast. The original 11.67-hour/17.66-GB estimate and its different basis are retained in the estimate JSON. Native evidence was not downsampled to meet a budget.
+
+Execution was real Windows desktop-local Python 3.13.5, Git 2.50.0.windows.1, NumPy 2.3.3, SciPy 1.16.2 and pytest 8.4.2. The existing isolated environment was reused; no dependencies were installed. Scoped local writes and the new code worktree were approved. Source design archive, all 55 reading copies and the 68-entry delivery payload were hash-verified. The prior artifact inventory contains 792 files; final preservation results are in `PRESERVATION_AFTER.json`.
+
+**Not tested or claimed:** A1–A5, B1–B4, C1, C2; a 600-second life; a new phase prehistory; controller navigation/recovery competence; human positive controls or perceptual-ceiling capability; blinded held-out trials or deprivation scenarios; long-run performance, storage growth or ten-second periodic-snapshot execution; commissioning sufficiency; survival, developmental utility or beneficial learning; scientific efficacy, population rates or an innate-maintenance result; fresh dependency installation or cross-platform identity; exhaustive contact convergence. No capacity sweep, parameter change, efficacy tuning, experiment number, scientific preregistration, push, PR, merge, vault Git write or ongoing background run was performed.
+
+Before any later commissioning, Jason must authorize exact starts/routes/phases, operator controls, resource limits and cases. Birth-specific verified caches must exist. The apparatus accepts a separately supplied authority-file identity scoped to the exact case, initial state and duration; none is delivered here. This is an auditable workflow guard, not an authentication system for the machine owner. Acceptance of a design or this ZIP is not that grant. Stop at apparatus review.
